{"title": "Sectional Mock #126 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>P is 10% more than Q and Q is 10% more than R. Then by what percent is P more than R?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P, Q &#2360;&#2375; 10% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Q, R &#2360;&#2375; 10% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; P, R &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["18.5%", "21%", "23%", "20%"], "options_hi": ["18.5%", "21%", "23%", "20%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let R = 100 units</p><p>Q = 100 * 110% = 110 units</p><p>P = 110 * 110% = 121 units</p><p>Required percentage = <img width=117 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20909/image019.png\"> = 21%</p><p><b>Alternate method:</b></p><p>Required percentage = 10 + 10 + <img width=52 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20909/image020.png\"> = 21%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let R = 100 units</p><p>Q = 100 * 110% = 110 units</p><p>P = 110 * 110% = 121 units</p><p>Required percentage = <img width=117 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20909/image019.png\"> = 21%</p><p><b>Alternate method:</b></p><p>Required percentage = 10 + 10 + <img width=52 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20909/image020.png\"> = 21%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;A boat can cover 30 km in still water in 5 hours and speed of the stream is <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;, &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; 1/2 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 57 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20 hours", "19 hours", "26 hours", "10 hours"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "19 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "26 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of boat in still water = 30/5 = 6 km/h</p><p>Speed of stream = 6 * 1/2 = 3 km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in upstream = 6 - 3 = 3 km/h</p><p>Time taken by the boat to cover 57 km in upstream = 57/3 = 19 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of boat in still water = 30/5 = 6 km/h</p><p>Speed of stream = 6 * 1/2 = 3 km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in upstream = 6 - 3 = 3 km/h</p><p>Time taken by the boat to cover 57 km in upstream = 57/3 = 19 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The perimeter of a circle and a square is same. If the radius of the circle is 28 cm, then find the area of the square (in cm<sup>2</sup>).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;/&#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 28 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1936", "784", "1156", "1369"], "options_hi": ["1936", "784", "1156", "1369"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The radius of the circle = 28 cm</p><p>Perimeter of circle = Perimeter of square</p><p>2*22/7 * 28 = 4*side</p><p>Side = 44 cm</p><p>So, the area of the square = 44*44 = 1936 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The radius of the circle = 28 cm</p><p>Perimeter of circle = Perimeter of square</p><p>2*22/7 * 28 = 4*side</p><p>Side = 44 cm</p><p>So, the area of the square = 44*44 = 1936 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many 5-digits numbers are there in which all digits are prime?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; 5-&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["1536", "1024", "1225", "1386"], "options_hi": ["1536", "1024", "1225", "1386"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>Let the 5-digit number = abcde</p><p>Digit used in place of 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd' and 'e' = 2, 3, 5 and 7 = 4 numbers</p><p>Therefore, total number of 5-digit numbers in which all digits are prime</p><p>= 4 * 4 * 4 * 4 * 4</p><p><b>= 1024</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>Let the 5-digit number = abcde</p><p>Digit used in place of 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd' and 'e' = 2, 3, 5 and 7 = 4 numbers</p><p>Therefore, total number of 5-digit numbers in which all digits are prime</p><p>= 4 * 4 * 4 * 4 * 4</p><p><b>= 1024</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a person spends 35% of his monthly income on his rent, 20% of the rest of the income on food, 25% of the remaining income on shopping, and he saves the remaining Rs. 1950, then find the monthly income.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 35% &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 20% &#2349;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 25% &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2361; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2352;&#2369;.1950 &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 5400", "Rs. 5000", "Rs. 6400", "Rs. 7200"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 5400", "&#2352;&#2369;. 5000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 6400", "&#2352;&#2369;. 7200"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the income be '100'.</p><p><img width=463 height=128 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24801/image004.jpg\" ></p><p>39 = Rs. 1950 </p><p>1 = 50 </p><p>Hence, monthly income = 50 * 100 = Rs. 5000 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the income be '100'.</p><p><img width=463 height=128 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24801/image004.jpg\" ></p><p>39 = Rs. 1950 </p><p>1 = 50 </p><p>Hence, monthly income = 50 * 100 = Rs. 5000 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the perimeter of a square to a rectangle is 8: 7 and the side of the square is equal to the length of the rectangle. If the breadth of the rectangle is 27 cm, then find the area of the rectangle. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 8: 7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["918 cm<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>945 cm<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>999 cm<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>972 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["918 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>945 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>999 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "<sup> </sup>972 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The perimeter of a square = 4 * side</p><p>The perimeter of a rectangle = 2 (Length + Breadth) </p><p>The perimeter of the square/ The perimeter of a rectangle = 8/ 7</p><p>4 * side/ [2 * (L + B) = 8/7</p><p>2 * L/ (L + 27) = 8/7 </p><p>L * 7 = 4 (L + 27) </p><p>3L = 4 * 27 </p><p>L = 36 cm</p><p>Hence, the area of the rectangle = 27 * 36 = 972 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The perimeter of a square = 4 * side</p><p>The perimeter of a rectangle = 2 (Length + Breadth) </p><p>The perimeter of the square/ The perimeter of a rectangle = 8/ 7</p><p>4 * side/ [2 * (L + B) = 8/7</p><p>2 * L/ (L + 27) = 8/7 </p><p>L * 7 = 4 (L + 27) </p><p>3L = 4 * 27 </p><p>L = 36 cm</p><p>Hence, the area of the rectangle = 27 * 36 = 972 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Arvind and Chetan started running simultaneously from the same point in the same direction on a circular track of length 210 m. If Arvind takes 180 seconds to complete one round, and Chetan takes 420 seconds to complete one round, after how much time will they meet for the first time at the starting point on the track?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2309;&#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; 210 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2352;&#2357;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 180 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 420 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?", "options_en": ["10 minutes", "15 minutes", "21 minutes", "28 minutes"], "options_hi": ["10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306;", "15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306;", "21 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "28 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Find LCM of 180 and 420.</p><p>Prime factorization of 180 = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3<sup>2</sup>  X  5</p><p>Prime factorization of 420 = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3  X  5  X  7</p><p>LCM = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3<sup>2</sup>  X  5  X  7</p><p>=&gt; 4  X  9  X  5  X  7 = 1260 seconds</p><p>Convert 1260 seconds to minutes:</p><p>=&gt; 1260 / 60 = 21 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Find LCM of 180 and 420.</p><p>Prime factorization of 180 = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3<sup>2</sup>  X  5</p><p>Prime factorization of 420 = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3  X  5  X  7</p><p>LCM = 2<sup>2</sup>  X  3<sup>2</sup>  X  5  X  7</p><p>=&gt; 4  X  9  X  5  X  7 = 1260 seconds</p><p>Convert 1260 seconds to minutes:</p><p>=&gt; 1260 / 60 = 21 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following pair of numbers is co-prime?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2309;&#2360;&#2361;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(88, 81)", "(29, 87)", "(33, 39)", "(45, 48)"], "options_hi": ["(88, 81)", "(29, 87)", "(33, 39)", "(45, 48)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>HCF of 88 and 81 = 1</p><p>HCF of 29 and 87 = 29</p><p>HCF of 33 and 39 = 3</p><p>HCF of 45 and 48 = 3</p><p>Hence (88, 81) is co-prime.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>HCF of 88 and 81 = 1</p><p>HCF of 29 and 87 = 29</p><p>HCF of 33 and 39 = 3</p><p>HCF of 45 and 48 = 3</p><p>Hence (88, 81) is co-prime.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 12% of 75% of 80% of a = 18, then which of the following is true?</p><p>I. 4% of 18% of a = 2.4</p><p>II. 30% of a% of 1200 = 720</p><p>III. 6% of a = 21</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 12% of 75% of 80% of a = 18 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>I. 4% of 18% of a = 2.4</p><p>II. 30% of a% of 1200 = 720</p><p>III. 6% of a = 21</p>", "options_en": ["Only I", "Only III", "Only II", "None of these"], "options_hi": ["&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; III", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II", "&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>12% of 75% of 80% of a = 18</p><p>(12/100) * (75/100) * (80/100) * a = 18</p><p>a = 250</p><p><b>From I: </b>4% of 18% of a</p><p>= (4/100) * (18/100) * 250</p><p>= 1.8 &#8800; 2.4</p><p><b>From II:</b> 30% of a% of 1200</p><p>= (30/100) * (250/100) * 1200</p><p>= 900 &#8800; 720</p><p><b>From III: </b>6% of a</p><p>= (6/100) * 250</p><p>= 15 &#8800; 21</p><p>Hence, option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>12% of 75% of 80% of a = 18</p><p>(12/100) * (75/100) * (80/100) * a = 18</p><p>a = 250</p><p><b>From I: </b>4% of 18% of a</p><p>= (4/100) * (18/100) * 250</p><p>= 1.8 &#8800; 2.4</p><p><b>From II:</b> 30% of a% of 1200</p><p>= (30/100) * (250/100) * 1200</p><p>= 900 &#8800; 720</p><p><b>From III: </b>6% of a</p><p>= (6/100) * 250</p><p>= 15 &#8800; 21</p><p>Hence, option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train crosses a pole and platform in 17 seconds and 42 seconds respectively. If the length of the platform is 200m then what is the length of the train?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2324;&#2352; 42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["125m", "98m", "120m", "136m"], "options_hi": ["125&#2350;&#2368;", "98&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "120&#2350;&#2368;", "136&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length and speed of the train be p meters and v m/s respectively.</p><p>Since the trains crosses a pole in 17 seconds</p><p>p = 17v ------ (1)</p><p>The train crosses a platform in 42 seconds</p><p>200 + p = 42v -------- (2)</p><p>On solving equation (1) and (2) we get-</p><p>v = 200/25 = 8 m/sec </p><p>p = 17  X  8 = 136 m</p><p>Therefore, the length of the train = 136 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length and speed of the train be p meters and v m/s respectively.</p><p>Since the trains crosses a pole in 17 seconds</p><p>p = 17v ------ (1)</p><p>The train crosses a platform in 42 seconds</p><p>200 + p = 42v -------- (2)</p><p>On solving equation (1) and (2) we get-</p><p>v = 200/25 = 8 m/sec </p><p>p = 17  X  8 = 136 m</p><p>Therefore, the length of the train = 136 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two circles with centres W and V touch each other externally at point X. W is the centre of bigger circle and WV is produced to a point S. If STU is the common tangent to the circles at T and U where T is a point on the smaller circle, the ratio of radii of the circles is 9: 5 and SW = 84 cm, then what is the length of TU?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; W &#2324;&#2352; V &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; W &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; WV &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; S &#2340;&#2325; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; STU, T &#2324;&#2352; U &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; T &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 5 &#2324;&#2352; SW = 84 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; TU &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12&radic;5 cm", "18&radic;5 cm", "20&radic;5 cm", "16&radic;5 cm"], "options_hi": ["12&radic;5 cm", "18&radic;5 cm", "20&radic;5 cm", "16&radic;5 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=376 height=136 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image015.jpg\"></p><p>Radius of larger circle = 9x cm</p><p>Radius of smaller circle = 5x cm</p><p>UT = &radic;[(9x + 5x)<sup>2</sup>  -  (9x  -  5x)<sup>2</sup> ] = &radic;(196x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;(180x<sup>2</sup>) = 6x&radic;5 cm</p><p>In &#8710;SVT and &#8710;SWU,</p><p>&#8736;STV = &#8736;SUW</p><p>&#8736;SVT = &#8736;SWU</p><p>Thus, &#8710;SVT ~ &#8710;SWU</p><p>VT/WU = SV/SW</p><p>=&gt; 5/9 = (84  -  14x)/84</p><p>=&gt; 84 * 5/9 = 84  -  14x</p><p>=&gt; 14x = 112/3</p><p>=&gt; x = 8/3</p><p>Hence, TU = 6&radic;5 * 8/3 = 16&radic;5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=376 height=136 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15951/image015.jpg\"></p><p>Radius of larger circle = 9x cm</p><p>Radius of smaller circle = 5x cm</p><p>UT = &radic;[(9x + 5x)<sup>2</sup>  -  (9x  -  5x)<sup>2</sup> ] = &radic;(196x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;(180x<sup>2</sup>) = 6x&radic;5 cm</p><p>In &#8710;SVT and &#8710;SWU,</p><p>&#8736;STV = &#8736;SUW</p><p>&#8736;SVT = &#8736;SWU</p><p>Thus, &#8710;SVT ~ &#8710;SWU</p><p>VT/WU = SV/SW</p><p>=&gt; 5/9 = (84  -  14x)/84</p><p>=&gt; 84 * 5/9 = 84  -  14x</p><p>=&gt; 14x = 112/3</p><p>=&gt; x = 8/3</p><p>Hence, TU = 6&radic;5 * 8/3 = 16&radic;5 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The table given below shows the average number of tourists visited in India and Japan together in five different years and the line graph shows the number of tourists visited in India.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Year</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Average number of tourists visited in India and Japan together</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2014</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2015</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2016</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2017</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2018</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">8000</td></tr></table><p><img width=416 height=246 id=\"Chart 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25169/image007.png\">.</p><p>What is the ratio of number of tourists visited in India in 2014 and 2015 together to number of tourists visited in Japan in 2018?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2335;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2335;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2335;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2014</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2015</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2016</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2017</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5000</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2018</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">8000</td></tr></table><p><img width=416 height=246 id=\"Chart 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25169/image007.png\">.</p><p>2014 &#2324;&#2352; 2015 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2310;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2335;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 2018 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2335;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7:8", "5:9", "8:3", "3:4"], "options_hi": ["7:8", "5:9", "8:3", "3:4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Number of tourists visited in India in 2014 and 2015 together = 5000 + 2500 = 7500</p><p>Number of tourists visited in Japan in 2018 = 2*8000  -  6000 = 10000</p><p>Required ratio = 7500:10000 = 3:4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of tourists visited in India in 2014 and 2015 together = 5000 + 2500 = 7500</p><p>Number of tourists visited in Japan in 2018 = 2*8000  -  6000 = 10000</p><p>Required ratio = 7500:10000 = 3:4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a parallelogram, 'a' and 'b' are adjacent sides, and its area is 108 cm<sup>2</sup>. If distance between two parallel sides, whose length is 'a', is 6 cm and the ratio of 'a' to 'b' is 9: 4, then find the perimeter of the parallelogram?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 'a' &#2324;&#2352; 'b' &#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 108 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;<sup>2</sup>&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 'a' &#2361;&#2376;, &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'a' &#2360;&#2375; 'b' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["48 cm", "60 cm", "44 cm", "52 cm"], "options_hi": ["48 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "44 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "52 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Area of the parallelogram = 108 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>So,</p><p>a * 6 = 108</p><p>a = 18 cm</p><p>Since, ratio of 'a' to 'b' = 9: 4</p><p>So,</p><p>b = 18 * (4/9) = 8 cm</p><p>Now, perimeter of the parallelogram = 2 * (18 + 8) = 52 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of the parallelogram = 108 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>So,</p><p>a * 6 = 108</p><p>a = 18 cm</p><p>Since, ratio of 'a' to 'b' = 9: 4</p><p>So,</p><p>b = 18 * (4/9) = 8 cm</p><p>Now, perimeter of the parallelogram = 2 * (18 + 8) = 52 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three runners M, N, and O jog around a circular track and complete one round in 15, 30, and 40 seconds respectively. In how many minutes will all the three meet again at the starting point?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2343;&#2366;&#2357;&#2325; M, N, &#2324;&#2352; O &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 15, 30, &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2344;&#2307; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["2 minutes", "4 minutes", "3 minutes", "5 minutes"], "options_hi": ["2 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "4 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Required time = LCM of 15, 30, and 40 = 120 seconds = 2 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Required time = LCM of 15, 30, and 40 = 120 seconds = 2 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>How can Two-Third of 15% be written in decimal form?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>15% &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379;-&#2340;&#2368;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["0.1", "0.01", "1.0", "10"], "options_hi": ["0.1", "0.01", "1.0", "10"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>According to Question,</p><p>Two-Third of 15%= 2/3<sup>rd</sup> of 15%</p><p>=2/3 x 15/100</p><p>=10/100</p><p>=1/10</p><p>=0.1 Ans.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to Question,</p><p>Two-Third of 15%= 2/3<sup>rd</sup> of 15%</p><p>=2/3 x 15/100</p><p>=10/100</p><p>=1/10</p><p>=0.1 Ans.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>At an event there are 500 guests, among whom 28% are adult males, 64% are adult females, and the rest are children. Find the total number of children at the event.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 500 &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2341;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 28% &#2357;&#2351;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;, 64% &#2357;&#2351;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["55", "45", "40", "50"], "options_hi": ["55", "45", "40", "50"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Percentage of children at the event = (100  -  28  -  64) = 8%</p><p>Number of children at the event = 0.08  X  500 = 40</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Percentage of children at the event = (100  -  28  -  64) = 8%</p><p>Number of children at the event = 0.08  X  500 = 40</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The base of a solid pyramid is square shaped with 75 cm long side. If height of the pyramid is 20 cm, then find the lateral surface area of the pyramid.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 75 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 20 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6062.5 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6250 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6125 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6375 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["6062.5 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6250 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6125 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6375 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Perimeter of the base = 4 * 75 = 300 cm</p><p>Slant height of the pyramid = &radic;((75/2)<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>) = 42.5 cm</p><p>So, lateral surface area of the pyramid = 1/2 * Perimeter * slant height = &frac12; * 300 * 42.5 = 6375 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Perimeter of the base = 4 * 75 = 300 cm</p><p>Slant height of the pyramid = &radic;((75/2)<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>) = 42.5 cm</p><p>So, lateral surface area of the pyramid = 1/2 * Perimeter * slant height = &frac12; * 300 * 42.5 = 6375 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the number of trailing zeros in 12345!?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>12345! &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3082", "3080", "3081", "3079"], "options_hi": ["3082", "3080", "3081", "3079"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>12345 mod 5 = 2469</p><p>12345 mod 25 = 493</p><p>12345 mod 125 = 98</p><p>12345 mod 625 = 19</p><p>12345 mod 3125 = 3</p><p>Total = 2469 + 493 + 98 + 19 + 3 = 3082</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>12345 mod 5 = 2469</p><p>12345 mod 25 = 493</p><p>12345 mod 125 = 98</p><p>12345 mod 625 = 19</p><p>12345 mod 3125 = 3</p><p>Total = 2469 + 493 + 98 + 19 + 3 = 3082</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two athletes are participating in a race on a circular track of 220 m. Ravi runs at the speed of 22 m/s, while Kapil runs at the speed of 11 m/s. They start from the same point, at the same time and in the same direction. After how many seconds will they meet for the first time<i>?</i></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2319;&#2341;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335; 220 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2352;&#2357;&#2367; 22 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2325;&#2346;&#2367;&#2354; 11 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 seconds", "16 seconds", "20 seconds", "24 seconds"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 22  -  11 = 11 m/s</p><p>Time = 220 / 11 = 20 seconds</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 22  -  11 = 11 m/s</p><p>Time = 220 / 11 = 20 seconds</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The speed of the boat downstream is 'a' km/hr and the speed of the boat upstream is (a  -  18) km/hr. Find the speed of the stream. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 'a' km/hr &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; (a - 18) km/hr &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6 km/hr", "4 km/hr", "8 km/hr", "9 km/hr"], "options_hi": ["6 km/hr", "4 km/hr", "8 km/hr", "9 km/hr"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of the stream = (1/2) [Downstream speed - upstream speed]</p><p>= (1/2) * [a - a + 18]</p><p>= 9 kmph</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of the stream = (1/2) [Downstream speed - upstream speed]</p><p>= (1/2) * [a - a + 18]</p><p>= 9 kmph</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Read the data carefully and answer the following question:</p><p>Below pie chart shows the percentage distribution of cars manufactured in five factories:</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 1986300170\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22337/image002.png\"></p><p>If the total number of cars manufactured in factory E and that in factory B is 12300, then how many cars manufactured in factory D?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2346;&#2397;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;:</p><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2326;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 1986300170\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22337/image002.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2326;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; E &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2326;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 12300 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2326;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; D &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["5200", "5400", "5600", "5000"], "options_hi": ["5200", "5400", "5600", "5000"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of cars manufactured in all five factories = 12300 * 100/(27 + 14) = 30000</p><p>Hence, number of cars manufactured in factory D = 18/100 * 30000 = 5400</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of cars manufactured in all five factories = 12300 * 100/(27 + 14) = 30000</p><p>Hence, number of cars manufactured in factory D = 18/100 * 30000 = 5400</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The square of one natural number is 39 greater than that of another natural number and their difference is 3. What is the value of 25% of their sum?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 39 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; 25% &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2.25", "3.25", "2.75", "3.75"], "options_hi": ["2.25", "3.25", "2.75", "3.75"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the larger and the smaller numbers be 'x' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup> = 39 and x  -  y = 3</p><p>So, x + y = (x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup>)/(x  -  y) = 39/3 = 13</p><p>25% of (x + y) = 13/4 = 3.25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the larger and the smaller numbers be 'x' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup> = 39 and x  -  y = 3</p><p>So, x + y = (x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup>)/(x  -  y) = 39/3 = 13</p><p>25% of (x + y) = 13/4 = 3.25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of a rhombus is 336 cm<sup>2</sup> and sum of its diagonal is 62 cm. What is the side of the rhombus? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 336 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 62 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "25 cm", "40 cm", "32 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "32 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the diagonal of the rhombus be 'd' cm and 'D' cm respectively.</p><p>D + d = 62 cm</p><p>Area of a rhombus = 336 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>&frac12; * d * D = 336</p><p>d*D = 672</p><p>Side of the rhombus = &radic;{(d/2)<sup>2</sup> + (D/2)<sup>2</sup>} </p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{d<sup>2</sup> + D<sup>2</sup>}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{(d+D)<sup>2</sup>  -  2dD}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{62<sup>2</sup>  -  2*672}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;(2500)</p><p>= &frac12; * 50</p><p>= 25 cm</p><p><u> </u></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the diagonal of the rhombus be 'd' cm and 'D' cm respectively.</p><p>D + d = 62 cm</p><p>Area of a rhombus = 336 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>&frac12; * d * D = 336</p><p>d*D = 672</p><p>Side of the rhombus = &radic;{(d/2)<sup>2</sup> + (D/2)<sup>2</sup>} </p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{d<sup>2</sup> + D<sup>2</sup>}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{(d+D)<sup>2</sup>  -  2dD}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;{62<sup>2</sup>  -  2*672}</p><p>= &frac12; * &radic;(2500)</p><p>= &frac12; * 50</p><p>= 25 cm</p><p><u> </u></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>When f(m) = m<sup>5 </sup>+ 5m<sup>4</sup> - 3m + 7 is divided by (m - 2), then the remainder is _____.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; f(m) = m<sup>5 </sup>+ 5m<sup>4</sup> - 3m + 7 &#2325;&#2379; (m - 2) &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; _____ &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7", "5", "0", "113"], "options_hi": ["7", "5", "0", "113"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Substitute m = 2 in f(m)</p><p>f(2) = 2<sup>5</sup> + 5(2<sup>4</sup>) - 3(2) + 7</p><p>=&gt; 32 + 5(16) - 6 + 7 = 32 + 80 - 6 + 7</p><p>=&gt; f(2) = 113</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Substitute m = 2 in f(m)</p><p>f(2) = 2<sup>5</sup> + 5(2<sup>4</sup>) - 3(2) + 7</p><p>=&gt; 32 + 5(16) - 6 + 7 = 32 + 80 - 6 + 7</p><p>=&gt; f(2) = 113</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>On a 450 m long circular track, two people start from the same point, at the same time, at speeds of 36 km/h and 54 km/h, respectively. After how much time will they meet at the starting point for the first time after:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>450 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 54 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;:</p>", "options_en": ["90 sec", "30 sec", "120 sec", "150 sec"], "options_hi": ["90 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "120 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "150 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>36 km/h = 36 x 5/18 = 10 m/s</p><p>54 km/h = 54 x 5/18 = 15 m/s</p><p>Time taken by them to complete 450 m alone = 450/10 = 45 sec and 450/15 = 30 sec.</p><p>Time taken by them to meet at the starting point for the first time after = LCM of 45 and 30 = 90 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>36 km/h = 36 x 5/18 = 10 m/s</p><p>54 km/h = 54 x 5/18 = 15 m/s</p><p>Time taken by them to complete 450 m alone = 450/10 = 45 sec and 450/15 = 30 sec.</p><p>Time taken by them to meet at the starting point for the first time after = LCM of 45 and 30 = 90 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}]}